---
title: Borsch
servings: 6
tags: [soup, beetroot, comfort food]
source: https://github.com/Gunde/recipes
---

Peel and grate the @beetroot{3}(medium), and peel and slice the @potatoes{3}(medium) and @carrots{3}. Keep the potato slices in cold water until needed so that they do not brown, then drain.

Heat @olive oil{2%tbsp} in a #large soup pot{} over a medium-high heat. Add the beetroot and cook for ~{10%minutes}, stirring now and then, until softened.

Add the @chicken stock{2%l} and @water{500%ml}, then the potatoes and carrots. Cook for ~{10-15%minutes}, until a fork slides in easily.

Meanwhile, heat @olive oil{2%tbsp} in a #large frying pan{} over a medium-high heat. Add the @onion{1}(medium, finely chopped), @celery{2%sticks}(chopped) and @bell pepper{1}(small, chopped) and cook for ~{7-8%minutes}, until soft and lightly golden. Stir in the @tomato paste{3%tbsp}, cook for ~{30%seconds} more, then tip everything into the soup pot.

When the potatoes and carrots are tender, add the @cannellini beans{400%g}(one tin, with its liquid), @bay leaves{2}, @distilled vinegar{2%tbsp}, @salt{1%tsp}, @black pepper{1/4%tsp}, @garlic{1%clove}(crushed) and @dill{3%tbsp}(chopped). Simmer for ~{2-3%minutes}, then taste and add more salt or vinegar as needed.
